<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-9638] .NET: JVM keeps track of CLR Threads, even when they are finished </title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-9638</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When you create a Thread in C#, JVM creates corresponding thread &quot;Thread-NNNN&quot; which is visible in jstack. When C# joins this thread, it is not removed from JVM and is kept around. This means that jstack may show thousands of threads which are not there. Reproducer is attached. It is presumed that memory will be exhausted eventually.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13185804">IGNITE-9638</key>
            <summary>.NET: JVM keeps track of CLR Threads, even when they are finished </summary>
